  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 7.1</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Gif he losige, ⁊ hine mon eft gefó, forgielde he hine self á be his weregilde, ⁊ ðone gylt gebete, swa wer swa wite, swa he gewryht age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If he escapes and is caught afterwards, let him always pay for himself with his wergild, and recompense for that offense – either [with] wergild or fine – which he has committed.</ab>
        <ab type="secondTranslation" xml:lang="en">If he escapes and is subsequently arrested, he shall pay for himself by his own wergeld in every case; and he shall pay compensation for the offence—both wergeld and fine—according to the nature of the outrage he has perpetrated.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Gif he losige, ⁊ hine mon eft gefó, forgylde he hine selfne be his wergilde, ⁊ þone gylt gebete, swa wer swa wite, swa he gewryht age.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
